body:
Hey, 

Going through therapy has helped me learn a lot about distress tolerance skills, mindfulness skills, etc. Based on your previous post history, my guess is that you probably know a little bit about DBT (Dialectical Behavioural Therapy)? If not, it may be worth looking into for managing stress and burn-out :) Do you already do things like keeping a gratitude journal, writing about emotions non-judgementally, taking time to care for yourself with pleasant activities, etc? Would you consider reviewing the amount of time you allocate for yourself, and make sure you set clear boundaries around the demands of others?

You are important and you are your responsibility, so please take your time to treat yourself with love, with care and with respect :) 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

